# Line endings: LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means git stores LF (as always) *and* checks LF out, rather
# than converting to CRLF on Windows. That matters now that the frontend exists:
# Prettier is configured with `endOfLine: "lf"`, so a CRLF checkout would make
# `npm run format:check` fail on every file for a teammate on Windows while
# passing in CI — a confusing first hour for exactly the people we onboard.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
